# Grbl in laser mode. Written from Grbl's public laser-mode documentation
# (gnea/grbl, "Laser Mode"), no firmware source.
#
# The machine is expected to have laser mode on ($32=1), set in the
# firmware, so a change of power does not stop the move. That is not
# written in the job: $ settings stay in the controller. $30 is the S
# at 100% power, often 1000; OpenMakeBurn uses 1000 unless you say
# otherwise.
# G21 is mm, G90 absolute, G94 mm per minute (Grbl's feed). M5 leaves
# the laser off. G0 at the end goes back to the origin. $H homes, when
# the machine has endstops; it is not in the start code, so a job can
# begin from the origin you set.
family = laser
dialect = grbl
send = file
features = laser-power homing
start = G21 ; mm
start += G90 ; absolute
start += G94 ; mm per minute
start += M5 ; laser off
end = M5
end += G0 X0 Y0
